{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>And Moses was not able</b> etc. And although the verse says in parashat Mishpatim (Exodus 24:18) ״וַיָּבֹא מֹשֶׁה בְּתוֹךְ הֶעָנָן״, there it was after HaShem called to him — He endowed him with strength. Or it may say along these lines: <b>and Moses was not able</b> etc., and the reason is <b>for the cloud abode upon it</b>, and this state of being is not like the state described in parashat Mishpatim, for here <b>the glory of HaShem filled the Tabernacle</b>, unlike the cloud that he entered at Mount Sinai, where it says (Exodus 24:17): ״וּמַרְאֵה כְּבוֹד ה׳ כְּאֵשׁ אוֹכֶלֶת בְּרֹאשׁ הָהָר״, and immediately after: ״וַיָּבֹא מֹשֶׁה בְּתוֹךְ הֶעָנָן וַיַּעַל אֶל הָהָר״ — meaning, a place where the glory of HaShem did not dwell, unlike what is before us, where the glory of HaShem filled the Tabernacle, and he could not enter a place filled with His glory, may He be blessed." "<b>The portion of Pekudei is concluded; the book of Exodus is finished.</b>" "<b>The portion of Pekudei is concluded; the book of Exodus is finished.</b>"], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {2 "This is a duplicate of the colophon in comment 1; it appears twice in the source as given."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:37:25.160408984Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}